{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485). There is essentially zero evidence about whether the image modality carries any predictive signal for this task. This is the most fundamental design uncertainty: if image has no useful signal, the entire multimodal configuration space (~36 configs) becomes low-value, and budget should focus on RNA encoder/profile improvements. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the contribution of the image modality alone, keeping profile_setting identical to config_001 (singleprofile) so the comparison is clean—only the modality changes. ResNet50 is a standard, well-understood encoder, making this a fair first probe. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget with only one data point, the highest-information experiment is the one that partitions the configuration space most decisively. A strong image-only result would justify investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion strategies; a weak result would redirect all remaining budget toward RNA encoder and multiprofile exploration. No other single experiment reduces this level of uncertainty as efficiently, and it avoids simultaneously changing multiple design axes (unlike a multimodal config that would confound modality addition with fusion choice)."
}

